  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply by $\\frac{3}{4}$, we split the whole into $4$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $3$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/b8c4393a9c7616238262a1e63f90d5245a0346ca05c4152087e4c25900b7f99c.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{9}{20}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}\\times \\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{9}{20}.\n$$",
